## 7. Falsifiers and Guardrails

The route fails if any of the following occurs:

- the physical target complex orientation is independently forced to
  `theta+i t` with no conjugate presentation;
- the gerbe curvings cannot be promoted from their invariant `(1,1)` atlas to
  compatible holomorphic Deligne data;
- the local degree-three trivializations fail projective overlap descent;
- the two special fibers cannot be removed without changing the selected
  Chern, torsion or equivariance rows;
- the repaired rank-nine object contains a degree-zero proper spectral
  subobject or fails the G3D slope certificate.

No ordinary global positive-degree fiber line is asserted. No time-arrow,
HYM, differential Bianchi, Standard-Model prediction or UV-complete quantum
gravity claim follows from this theorem.

